  <text id="shot-label" x="70" y="144" width="712" height="14" font="caption" size="11" color="muted" align="center" wrap="false">Real web screenshot • browser-rendered parcel map with multiple markers, active legends, and corridor overlays</text>
  <shape id="right-card" type="rect" x="826" y="136" width="396" height="428" fill="surface" stroke="border" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="right-title" x="850" y="162" width="348" height="28" font="body" size="20" color="ink"><p><strong>What this unlocks for Kano</strong></p></text>
  <text id="right-copy" x="850" y="204" width="348" height="316" font="body" size="17" color="ink" line-height="1.33">
    <p>The map view helps Kano connect parcel identity, digitised land intelligence, and workflow context in one review environment.</p>
    <p space-before="14"><strong>This supports:</strong></p>
    <p space-before="10">• Better alignment between field demarcation and the registry record.</p>
    <p>• Clearer parcel context before certificate generation or post-title transactions.</p>
    <p>• A more practical GIS backbone for land administration and governance use cases.</p>
    <p>• Stronger visibility into corridor-sensitive infrastructure, housing, and extractive review zones.</p>
  </text>
  <shape id="assurance-band" type="rect" x="58" y="586" width="1164" height="40" fill="#ECFDF5" stroke="#BBF7D0" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="assurance" x="82" y="598" width="1116" height="16" font="body" size="15" color="ink" align="center" wrap="false">For Kano, parcel maps become more valuable when they directly support demarcation, certification, and revenue-linked registry continuity.</text>
